    pr_ref:  # 9b03
    description: "FOUND while fixing WI-gabuv (owner_ancestry, finalize sub-step 7d).\n\nSTATEMENT. Rails models are the Ruby analogue of `use Ecto.Repo`: `class User < ApplicationRecord` (`ApplicationRecord < ActiveRecord::Base`) called as `User.where(...)` / `User.find(1)` / `User.create(...)`. owner_ancestry stamps these calls (verified on a fixture: `ruby:User:0-0:where:external_symbol`, receiver_type_hint User), but (1) there is NO ruby io_primitives catalogue at all (io_primitives/ has no ruby.yaml and no overlay), so nothing can classify them; and (2) the stamped parent is `Base`, not `ActiveRecord::Base`: the extends edge is `ruby:external:0-0:Base:external_symbol`, the ruby analyzer having dropped the namespace of the external base (same family as WI-kazut). An unqualified `Base` would be a poor module key for any future row.\n\nFIX DIRECTION. (a) Keep the qualified external base name on the ruby extends edge (`ActiveRecord::Base`); (b) a ruby catalogue (at least an ActiveRecord community overlay: where/find/find_by/all/pluck/exists? as db_read; create/update/save/destroy/delete_all/update_all/insert_all as db_write; note `where` builds a lazy Relation -- ADR-0049's deferred-crossing ruling applies, like Ecto.Query). Not measured on a corpus repository (postal/mastodon/chatwoot are present locally)."  # 9b03
    fields: {}  # 9b03
